{sov: Notes}
Disco-Funk Classic: Built on standard 7th chord structures with a continuous
driving 16th-note rhythm pattern in F Mixolydian.

Iconic Speed-Up Intro Guitar Riff: Guitarist Jerome Smith recorded the opening
speed-picked solo at half-speed on reel-to-reel tape and sped it up an octave
for the final mix.

Rhythm Guitar: Play light, single-note funk scratches and tight 16th-note
vamps on F9 and Bb9 extended voicings using upper strings only.

Horn and Synth Lines: Horns supply heavy syncopated stabs on the beat while
the bass maintains a classic four-on-the-floor disco octave pattern.
{eov}